## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The problems

1. **`parser`** · [ticket #4](https://github.com/lbojalkowski-bf/mega-what-it-shows/issues/4):
   the shared parser reads every date month first, and day and month swap. This is the bug the
   queued fix is for.
2. **`hint`** · [ticket #2](https://github.com/lbojalkowski-bf/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2):
   the `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, so people at day-first tenants
   type month first. The parser fix does not touch it: the form's hint does.
3. **one-day move** · [ticket #1](https://github.com/lbojalkowski-bf/mega-what-it-shows/issues/1):
   the reports the desk read as a one-day move (the note under the table). A date converted
   between time zones, not a day/month swap; neither fix touches it.

## How the reports were counted

1. As the desk tagged them at intake: the "tagged as" column above.
2. The reports the desk read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`) go to their own ticket, not to
   the tag they came in with. Each report is counted once.

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Why one ticket hid two

Decision [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone. Reports about
different bugs use the same words ("Date is wrong"), so they landed in one ticket. Its own
consequence says engineering merges separate tickets later; nobody splits merged ones. A later
decision record should replace it: merge on cause (tenant, form, channel), not on subject.

